      "conf": "VERIFIED · WIRE",
      "dek": "The VIX, the market's fear gauge, closed at 15.67, up 0.49 points on the day. It traded as high as 16.57 during the session and handed nearly all of that back, which is the options market saying it does not regard today's jump in borrowing costs as dangerous. On the BuyTrigger ladder, under 15 is calm, 15 to 20 normal, 20 to 30 nervous, and above 30 is the system's buy window. At 15.67 the gauge sits 0.67 above the calm line and 14.33 below that window. Nothing here is a signal; it is the quiet backdrop against which the next shock gets measured.",
