      "conf": "VERIFIED · PRIMARY",
      "dek": "Costco sold $93.9 billion of goods in its fourth quarter, 11.2% more than a year earlier, and earned $6.75 a share against $5.87. Read the footnote: 15 cents of that came from a one-off refund of IEEPA tariffs, so the underlying figure is $6.60. Strip out petrol prices and currency swings and sales at established warehouses grew 6.7%, not the 9.4% headline, which is still good but a different number. The quarter was 16 weeks against 16 weeks last year, so nothing is flattered by the calendar. The shares closed down 0.91% and did not move after hours, which says this was already expected.",
